        {
          "text": "What it is"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b2",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "E415 Xanthan gum is a polysaccharide produced by bacterial fermentation of sugars. It is used to thicken and stabilise the texture of foods."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "key": "b3",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why it is in your food"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b4",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Manufacturers use it as thickener/stabiliser."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "key": "b5",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What we hold on it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "key": "b6",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This page is about the record we hold on this additive: who has written about it, and where you can read them."
